      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start, it’s professional. But I just ran it through our internal tool and the positivity score came back a bit low—around 0.4. The client is actually a bit sensitive; they want the response to feel a bit more \"warm\" and \"welcoming\" rather than just a dry, cold apology. \n\nCan you try another version? Like I said before, please don't just go overboard with the adjectives or make it sound fake—that's the main thing we want to avoid—but maybe try to lean a bit more into the positive/welcoming side of things while still being sincere about the mistake?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
